  message: "Worked on branch jgstern-agent/fix/hojib (worktree ~/hg_wt/hojib), on top of WI-silos 41fd9834a6. Commits 952164dd8c, ef734925a8, eabbd346cd. Not pushed; the integrator merges it with WI-silos.\n\nPREMISE CORRECTION. On Alamofire f73a2fc `stored` is NOT a generic identity: Tests/BaseTestCase.swift:108 is `func stored(_ session: Session) -> Session`, called from SUBCLASSES of BaseTestCase. Its return type was in the registry under `BaseTestCase.stored`; the lookup never walked base classes. The base-class walk is fixed. XCTest's `expectation` is reached the same way, through a new community row file library_signatures/swift-xctest.yaml. The built-in swift.yaml was refused by the catalogue scope gate, because XCTest is not an OS framework.\n\nThe other shapes are typed by value: literals (default type); member chains through the head's DECLARED member, bases included (`config.fileManager`); `??` / `?:` when every operand agrees; `_T(...)`, `Self(...)`, `self.init()` and `T.init()`; `self.m()` as `m()`.\n\nTests: test_swift_initialiser_shapes.py was red on the silos tree, is green now, and was mutation-checked. Final targeted smart-test: 15688 passed, 0 failed, `All changed source files are at 100% coverage`, exit 0.\n\nA/B on 4 frozen repos (A = origin/dev 385ec63be1, S = silos, B = silos+hojib):\n- 141 of the 272 sites where silos removed a stamp come back; a read of 20 found 20 right.\n- Kingfisher's 3 catalogued FileManager chains return, plus 5 more `config.fileManager` chains. total_io_edges 63 -> 60 -> 68.\n- vapor gains 19 catalogued chains; none is lost on any repo.\n\nRecord: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/hojib.md (OUTCOME, CLOSURE NOTE, every changed class sampled)."  # c57c
